# Regression script for the Speak About hand-off (see NarrativeController.StartObservationPhaseWithHistory).
# Run: dotnet run -- --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 \
#        --no-encounters --period noon --cli-timeout 300 --cli-script cli/companion_handoff.cli 2>&1 | grep '^\[cli\]'
# A non-zero exit means an `expect`/`wait` failed.
#
# --fill-party is what makes this reachable: Speak About needs a companion, and recruiting one in play
# is a long approach. At seed 42 the party is filled with the cat Nighthunter, and the protagonist is
# Kenryc Greygate — both names are seed-stable, which is what the `expect`s below key on. The panel
# header names the ACTIVE member, so "[NIGHTHUNTER]" on screen is the assertion that the hand-off held.

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# The session opens on the protagonist.
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]

# Speak About: keyword -> "Speak About" -> speaking modus mentis -> companion.
# (The keyword is the observed object's own noun under --playground, not the word "attention".)
click keyword boulder
choose 2
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

# The address is ONE spoken block (call attention + describe + ask, merged into a single request),
# and the narration has passed to the companion.
expect come and look at this
expect [NIGHTHUNTER]

# The companion acts: their own thinking phase, action, dice, outcome.
strategy succeed
click keyword boulder
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# Footer CONTINUE closes the segment and opens a fresh observation phase in the same session:
# the old text greys into history, noetic points refill — and the companion KEEPS the narration.
# Resetting to the protagonist here is the bug this script exists for.
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
expect [NIGHTHUNTER]

quit
